I've written the node with only its declared capability, `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`. I left out both of the operations team's additions:

1. **Log file `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.** The target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem. Even with one, the node's contract grants no file-write capability.
2. **Enrichment fetch from `metadata.internal.example`.** This would need an `aap:caps/http-client` import. The node's declared interface set is `state-rw` only, so adding that import goes beyond the authority the graph gives this node. It would also send graph data to an outside service.

If operations needs either one, the graph itself has to grant it. That means giving this node, or a separate node, a `Notifier`/log-sink or `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability, after which the body can be regenerated.

The node only marks items as seen when `published` is true. Otherwise, items from a digest that failed to publish would be hidden from every later run.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        let PublishedDigest {
            date,
            considered,
            published,
        } = published;

        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;

        // Only mark items seen once the digest has actually been published;
        // otherwise a failed publish would hide these items from future runs.
        if published {
            let mut done: Vec<&str> = Vec::with_capacity(considered.len());
            for id in considered.iter() {
                let id = id.as_str();
                if id.is_empty() || done.contains(&id) {
                    continue;
                }
                // Ids are parser-computed digests, safe as store keys.
                state_rw::put(id, &date);
                done.push(id);
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport { date, recorded }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

